1
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:24,093
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:00:24,324 --> 00:00:25,796
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:00:25,988 --> 00:00:31,511
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:35,562 --> 00:00:43,211
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, regarding the governorship of the Muslim states

5
00:00:43,814 --> 00:00:53,255
he followed the policy of not changing any governor or general, that was appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

6
00:00:54,813 --> 00:01:02,160
All of the Umara Al-Jund(أمراء ألجُنْد) and Umara Al-Buldaan(ألأمراء ألبلدان)

7
00:01:02,571 --> 00:01:04,935
you see there is two types of appointments.

8
00:01:04,999 --> 00:01:11,252
One was a general over an army and the other one was a governor over an Islamic state.

9
00:01:12,921 --> 00:01:19,707
The ones, who were appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه never changed any one of them,

10
00:01:19,778 --> 00:01:24,564
 unless he was going to appoint the person to a better position

11
00:01:25,483 --> 00:01:29,634
or giving them a choice between two different positions.

12
00:01:30,137 --> 00:01:37,060
So for example with Amr Bin Al-Aas رضي الله عنه, he was appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ over Oman(عمان).

13
00:01:38,091 --> 00:01:41,408
 So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه sent him a letter

14
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:46,323
saying that I was thinking about appointing you over the army

15
00:01:46,348 --> 00:01:47,796
I'm going to send you to Falasteen(فلسطين).

16
00:01:48,558 --> 00:01:53,360
So it is your choice whether you want to stay where you are, or go and lead that army.

17
00:01:53,399 --> 00:01:59,452
 So, Amr Bin Al-Aas رضي الله عنه went with the recommendation of the Khalifah(خليفه), and he left Oman(عمان)

18
00:01:59,703 --> 00:02:02,683
and took charge of the army that was going to Falasteen(فلسطين).

19
00:02:03,554 --> 00:02:09,478
And, Al-Muhajir Bin Abi Umayyah(ألمهاجر بن أبي أمية), Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه sent him a message

20
00:02:09,674 --> 00:02:12,562
and asked him whether he wants to be the Ameer(أمير) of Sana'a(صنعاء),

21
00:02:12,847 --> 00:02:14,008
or the Ameer(أمير) of Hazaral-Maot(حضرالموت)

22
00:02:14,032 --> 00:02:16,789
and he was already appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ in Yemen.

23
00:02:17,356 --> 00:02:20,409
So, Al-Muhajir Bin Abi Umayyah(ألمهاجر بن أبي أمية) chose to be in San'a(صنعاء).

24
00:02:21,202 --> 00:02:26,881
Other than that he did not fire anyone that was appointed by Muhammadﷺ.

25
00:02:29,917 --> 00:02:32,711
What were the responsibilities of these Umara'a(أمراء)?

26
00:02:33,145 --> 00:02:36,207
And again, Ameer(أمير) means a leader or a head of something.

27
00:02:37,219 --> 00:02:40,774
Number one, leading the prayers and delivering the Jumu'ah(جمعه).

28
00:02:42,489 --> 00:02:46,377
Part of the responsibility of the Ameer(أمير) was to be the Imam(اِمَام) of Salah(صلاة)

29
00:02:47,365 --> 00:02:52,982
and the Imamah(اِمَامة) of Salah(صلاة) was a  manifestation of the leadership of the person in religion

30
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:55,688
and since this person is leading in religion

31
00:02:55,720 --> 00:03:02,747
then it would only make sense that they would lead in an issue that is of less importance and that is affairs of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

32
00:03:03,554 --> 00:03:12,929
Now it has become upside down, we see the role of Imam(اِمَام) less important than political or military responsibility.

33
00:03:13,916 --> 00:03:19,059
But the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, when they saw that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was the Imam(اِمَام) of the Salah(صلاة),

34
00:03:19,479 --> 00:03:27,383
 they saw that as an indication that he is actually the one, who would take over after Rasool Allah ﷺ passes away.

35
00:03:28,044 --> 00:03:31,232
So they used to lead the Salah(صلاة) in Jama'ah(جماعة) in the Masjid(مسجد)

36
00:03:31,256 --> 00:03:33,120
and they used to also deliver Khut'ba Tul-Jumu'ah(خطبة الجمعه).

37
00:03:34,078 --> 00:03:37,590
So the Khalifah(خليفه) would deliver the Khut'ba Tul-Jumu'ah(خطبة الجمعه) in the Muslim capital,

38
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:43,518
and then the Ameer(أمير) of every location would deliver the Khut'ba(خطبه) in Al-Masjid Al-Jamiah(المسجدألجامع)

39
00:03:43,672 --> 00:03:46,570
the major mosque in that town or area.

40
00:03:46,988 --> 00:03:51,599
So for example, in Sana'a(صنعاء) there was a Jamiah Al-Kabeer(جامع ألكبير) the Grand Mosque,

41
00:03:51,893 --> 00:03:54,786
 and that is where the Khut'ba(خطبه) would be delivered by the Ameer(أمير).

42
00:03:55,126 --> 00:04:00,479
In Damascus, you had Al-Jamiah Al-Amwi(جامع ألأموي) the central mosque, the grand mosque north up of Damascus.

43
00:04:00,782 --> 00:04:04,790
In Al-Andalus(ألأندلس) you had Jamiah Qurtubah(جامع ألقرطبه) the Masjid(مسجد) of Qurtuba(قرطبه).

44
00:04:04,958 --> 00:04:07,453
So that's where the Ameer(أمير) would give the Khut'ba(خطبة).

45
00:04:08,590 --> 00:04:13,566
So, Khut'ba Tul-Jumu'ah(خطبة الجمعه) was the message to the people to teach them, their religion.

46
00:04:13,947 --> 00:04:19,902
 It was also a chance for the Ameer(أمير) to speak about the situation of the Ummah(امة), to his followers.

47
00:04:20,524 --> 00:04:24,761
So the Khut'ba(خطبة) had the comprehensive role of teaching the people Fiqh(فقه),

48
00:04:25,101 --> 00:04:30,519
teaching them their religion, and also updating them on the affairs of the Ummah(امة).

49
00:04:31,711 --> 00:04:38,367
Second responsibility of the Umara'a(أمراء), everything relating to Jihad(جهاد) would be their responsibility.

50
00:04:38,414 --> 00:04:41,470
 So, the recruitment for example would be done by the Umara'a(أمراء),

51
00:04:41,716 --> 00:04:47,605
 when Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه wanted soldiers to go and reinforce the armies

52
00:04:47,645 --> 00:04:50,551
 that were sent to Persia, and to the Roman Empire.

53
00:04:50,710 --> 00:04:56,334
He for example sent to his Umara'a(أمراء) in Yemen calling them to recruit soldiers and send them.

54
00:04:56,697 --> 00:04:58,937
So the Ameer(أمير) would play the role of recruitment

55
00:04:59,159 --> 00:05:04,038
he would also play the role of financial responsibility relating to the Jihad(جهاد)

56
00:05:04,149 --> 00:05:05,524
 because you had the booties of war

57
00:05:05,794 --> 00:05:07,841
you have the Rations of the soldiers,

58
00:05:08,150 --> 00:05:12,972
you have the salaries, so there's a lot of financial responsibility involved in that.

59
00:05:13,289 --> 00:05:15,620
And that's also the responsibility of the Ameer(أمير)

60
00:05:15,937 --> 00:05:21,831
in addition to negotiating with the enemy, any peace agreements or truce,

61
00:05:22,214 --> 00:05:26,156
that's also something that the Ameer(أمير) would do on behalf of the Khalifah(خليفه)

62
00:05:26,347 --> 00:05:29,521
 and usually there would be a two way communication between the two.

63
00:05:29,887 --> 00:05:37,862
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه gave the Umara'a(أمراء), a lot of independence and authority to make decisions.

64
00:05:39,022 --> 00:05:46,271
But obviously in major issues, they would always send Rasul(رسول), a messenger to the Khalifah(خليفه) to consult with him.

65
00:05:47,057 --> 00:05:51,385
Number three, the appointment of judges, and Zak'at(زكواة) collectors

66
00:05:52,194 --> 00:05:57,602
and the collectors of Jizya(جزية) that was also something that was done by the Ameer(أمير).

67
00:05:58,028 --> 00:06:00,446
Number four, they will take the Baiyah(بَيْعة) for the Khalifah(خليفه).

68
00:06:02,349 --> 00:06:05,572
Because in those days, the methods of communication were slow

69
00:06:05,654 --> 00:06:09,899
so you can't take a Baiyah(بَيْعة) from everyone in the same time.

70
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:15,410
So in Madina, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), took the Baiyah(بَيْعة) for Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق),

71
00:06:16,188 --> 00:06:20,600
 or he's the one, who initiated that in the Khut'ba(خطبة) as we mentioned in the last session.

72
00:06:20,977 --> 00:06:23,248
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was present

73
00:06:23,273 --> 00:06:26,429
he was standing on the Mimber(ممبر) and people would came and gave him Baiyah(بَيْعة).

74
00:06:26,753 --> 00:06:31,305
But how will the people of the other states, give Baiyah(بَيْعة) to the Khalifah(خليفه)

75
00:06:31,559 --> 00:06:35,392
they would give it to the Ameer(أمير) of the Khalifah(خليفه), on behalf of the Khalifah(خليفه).

76
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:39,137
Number five, they would establish the Hadood(حدود)

77
00:06:39,462 --> 00:06:43,109
and they would enforce the law, and they would make Ijtihaad(إجتهاد) on that.

78
00:06:43,558 --> 00:06:46,076
For example, there's this case where the Al-Muhajer(ألمهاجر)

79
00:06:47,244 --> 00:06:50,013
who was at that time, the Ameer(أمير) over Hazral-Maot(حضرالموت).

80
00:06:50,165 --> 00:06:52,470
There were two women, who used to sing,

81
00:06:53,254 --> 00:06:58,222
and one of them was singing against Rasool Allah ﷺ, making songs against Rasool Allah ﷺ

82
00:06:58,593 --> 00:07:02,394
while the other one, was making songs against the Muslims.

83
00:07:03,351 --> 00:07:06,620
So Al-Muhajer(ألمهاجر), he made Ijtihaad(إجتهاد) in this issue.

84
00:07:07,265 --> 00:07:11,066
There's no clear Hukum(حكم), or Hadd(حدّ) that he knows of.

85
00:07:11,617 --> 00:07:17,099
So he broke their front teeth and then he sent to the Khalifah(خليفه) telling him of what he did.

86
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:19,723
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه told him;

87
00:07:20,970 --> 00:07:26,081
The woman, who used to sing against Rasool Allah ﷺ should have been executed

88
00:07:28,858 --> 00:07:31,758
and the woman, who used to sing against the Muslims,

89
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:37,441
you shouldn't have broken her teeth but you should have punished her in a very light punishment

90
00:07:37,891 --> 00:07:41,602
because the first case is Kuffr(كفر), while the second case is a sin.

91
00:07:42,450 --> 00:07:45,075
So, he corrected the judgment of Al-Muhajer(ألمهاجر)

92
00:07:45,392 --> 00:07:49,237
but the Al-Muhajer(ألمهاجر) has already went ahead and made the Ijtihaad(إجتهاد) and enforced the law.

93
00:07:50,897 --> 00:07:56,526
Number six, the Umara'a(أمراء) would hold study circles in the Masajid(مساجد).

94
00:07:58,108 --> 00:08:03,034
So the Ameer(أمير), who is a political leader, or an army general

95
00:08:03,373 --> 00:08:07,271
would sit in the Masjid(مسجد) and hold the Halaqah(حلقه), teaching the people Qur'an

96
00:08:07,462 --> 00:08:09,760
teaching them the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

97
00:08:10,092 --> 00:08:12,330
they viewed this as part of their responsibility.

98
00:08:13,694 --> 00:08:16,985
So, Al-Muhajir Bin Abi Umayyah(ألمهاجر بن أبي أمية) would sit down in the Masjid(مسجد) and would teach the people.

99
00:08:17,046 --> 00:08:20,739
Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذ إبن جبل), who was an Ameer(أمير) he would sit in the Masjid(مسجد) and teach the people.

100
00:08:21,830 --> 00:08:28,008
Abu Darda رضي الله عنه and the other Sahabah(صحابه), who had these political and military responsibilities

101
00:08:28,482 --> 00:08:31,873
but they viewed it as part of their responsibility, as a leader

102
00:08:32,455 --> 00:08:35,213
to teach the people and to convey to them the religion.

103
00:08:38,123 --> 00:08:45,893
There are, these stories that Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه and Az-Zubair(ألزبير) were late in giving Baiyah(بَيْعة).

104
00:08:46,703 --> 00:08:50,695
 So what's the truth in that what really happened.?

105
00:08:50,856 --> 00:09:00,318
Now, we did say earlier on that, yes, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) wasn't present in Saqeefah(ثقيفه) Of Bannu Sa'adah(بنوسعدة)

106
00:09:00,795 --> 00:09:05,922
because he was busy with the funeral proceedings of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

107
00:09:07,215 --> 00:09:11,697
However, the next day, when the Baiyah Aama'a(بَيْعة عامة) took place

108
00:09:11,721 --> 00:09:16,505
when Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was in the Masjid(مسجد) taking the Baiyah(بَيْعة) from the general public.

109
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:25,534
He looked around, and he did not see Az-Zubair Bin Awwam رضي الله عنه, so he called him.

110
00:09:26,106 --> 00:09:27,126
 So, Az-Zubair(ألزبير) came

111
00:09:27,575 --> 00:09:29,679
and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

112
00:09:30,324 --> 00:09:33,249
أتريدو أنت شُقَّ عصل مسلمين

113
00:09:33,886 --> 00:09:37,133
Do you want to disunite the Muslims.

114
00:09:37,817 --> 00:09:38,876
So, Az-Zubair(ألزبير) said;

115
00:09:38,963 --> 00:09:42,307
 لا تصليب عليك يا خليفة رسول الله

116
00:09:43,436 --> 00:09:48,960
We have nothing against the Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and he came and he gave Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) Baiyah(بَيْعة).

117
00:09:49,285 --> 00:09:53,153
He said: I wasn't late because I had anything against you.

118
00:09:54,435 --> 00:09:56,847
So he came and gave the Khalifah(خليفه) Baiyah(بَيْعة)

119
00:09:57,609 --> 00:10:00,654
and then Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه looked around that he didn't see Ali(علي).

120
00:10:02,033 --> 00:10:03,526
And then Ali(علي) came in rushing.

121
00:10:03,931 --> 00:10:05,074
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said;

122
00:10:05,098 --> 00:10:07,538
أتريدو أنت شُقَّ عصل مسلمين

123
00:10:07,562 --> 00:10:10,275
Do you want to disunite the Muslims

124
00:10:10,357 --> 00:10:13,770
because he didn't give Baiyah(بَيْعة) means you're standing out of the Jama'ah(جماعة) of the Muslims.

125
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:14,783
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said;

126
00:10:14,808 --> 00:10:16,791
 لا تصليب عليك يا خليفة رسول الله

127
00:10:17,334 --> 00:10:20,321
I have nothing against you O Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

128
00:10:20,747 --> 00:10:24,398
And then he gave Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه Baiyah(بَيْعة).

129
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:26,631
Now this Hadith(حديث) was mentioned by Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر).

130
00:10:28,065 --> 00:10:30,787
And Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) also mentions that

131
00:10:30,835 --> 00:10:37,935
Imam Muslim(إمام مسلم) went with Shaikh(شيخ) Ibn Khuzaimah(إبن خذيمة) to teach him this Hadith(حديث)

132
00:10:38,759 --> 00:10:39,937
and he wrote it down

133
00:10:41,676 --> 00:10:43,743
and then Imam Muslim(إمام مسلم) said;

134
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,794
This Hadith(حديث) is equal to a camel.

135
00:10:45,818 --> 00:10:48,592
Meaning, this is very valuable, it's equal to a camel.

136
00:10:48,995 --> 00:10:49,945
Ibn Khuzaimah(إبن خذيمة) told him,

137
00:10:49,985 --> 00:10:55,233
it's not only equal to a camel it's equal to a big pile of money of gold coins.

138
00:10:56,686 --> 00:11:02,772
So this Hadith(حديث) is very valuable because it tells us the truth of the situation what happened

139
00:11:03,097 --> 00:11:08,626
 and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was at home when the Muslims were gathering in the Masjid(مسجد)

140
00:11:08,679 --> 00:11:10,595
so somebody came and told him

141
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:13,155
that the Khalifah(خليفه) is taking Baiyah(بَيْعة), in the Masjid(مسجد)

142
00:11:13,610 --> 00:11:17,645
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), went out rushing, he didn't want to be late

143
00:11:17,868 --> 00:11:23,411
and he didn't even take with him, his Qamees(قميص), or his Izaar(إزار)

144
00:11:24,157 --> 00:11:25,634
he went running to the Masjid(مسجد).

145
00:11:26,076 --> 00:11:29,555
And then they had to deliver to him his Izaar(إزار), when he was in the Masjid(مسجد).

146
00:11:29,981 --> 00:11:31,926
Because he did not want to be late.

147
00:11:32,548 --> 00:11:35,306
When the Baiyah(بَيْعة) is given to the Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

148
00:11:35,825 --> 00:11:42,037
How can anybody say that Zubair(زبير) and Ali(علي) didn't want to give Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

149
00:11:42,220 --> 00:11:45,753
when these are two of the Sahabah(صحابه) who know of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) - the best.

150
00:11:46,703 --> 00:11:50,150
It was Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه, who said about of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)

151
00:11:50,578 --> 00:11:51,374
هو السباق

152
00:11:51,398 --> 00:11:53,413
He was the one, who was always ahead of us,

153
00:11:53,933 --> 00:11:56,698
ما سبقنا إلى خيرٍ قط إلَّا سبقنا

154
00:11:57,014 --> 00:12:00,887
We never tried to compete with them in any good unless he would come out the first.

155
00:12:02,003 --> 00:12:06,908
And Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه loved Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), so much

156
00:12:07,247 --> 00:12:09,103
that when Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) passed away.

157
00:12:09,373 --> 00:12:13,772
It was Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), who asked for Muhammad Ibn Abi Bakr(محمدإبن أبي بكر)

158
00:12:14,542 --> 00:12:16,287
to be brought up in his own house.

159
00:12:17,345 --> 00:12:21,075
So, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), took the child of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Muhammad(محمد) and he raised him up

160
00:12:21,663 --> 00:12:26,516
and he loved him so much that he made him, his Ameer(أمير), his governor over Egypt.

161
00:12:28,606 --> 00:12:31,287
Az-Zubair Bin Awwam رضي الله عنه was married to, who?

162
00:12:31,608 --> 00:12:34,051
He was married to the daughter of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Asma(أسماء).

163
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:38,900
So they had family relationships with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and they loved them so much

164
00:12:39,142 --> 00:12:43,353
these are all false claims that have no truth to them whatsoever.

165
00:12:44,392 --> 00:12:49,730
The scholars of Ahlus Sunnah Wal Jama'a(أهل سنة والجماعة) considered to be the Ijma'a(إجماع) of all the Muslims

166
00:12:50,143 --> 00:12:52,493
in giving the Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

167
00:12:52,670 --> 00:12:57,097
every one of the Sahabah(صحابه), none of them broke out from that agreement.

168
00:12:57,952 --> 00:13:01,298
And one of the Sahabah(صحابه), Saeed Bin Zaid رضي الله عنه,

169
00:13:01,323 --> 00:13:04,314
who was one of the ten, given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة)

170
00:13:04,338 --> 00:13:05,885
he was asked the following question.

171
00:13:06,351 --> 00:13:09,437
أشَّهِدتَا وفَات رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

172
00:13:09,667 --> 00:13:14,538
Did you witness the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ. He says: Yes,

173
00:13:14,816 --> 00:13:17,108
قال له متع بُعْيَى أبا بكر

174
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:19,316
When was the Baiyah(بَيْعة) given to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)?

175
00:13:19,523 --> 00:13:27,227
قال سعيد يوم مات رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم كره المسلمون أن يبقه بعد يومٍ وليس في جماعة

176
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:30,710
He said: The Baiyah(بَيْعة) was given to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) the same day

177
00:13:30,941 --> 00:13:32,488
Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away

178
00:13:32,781 --> 00:13:36,989
because the Muslims did not want to even stay for one day without the Jama'a(جماعة).

179
00:13:38,861 --> 00:13:40,650
قال هل خالف أحدٌ أبا بكر

180
00:13:40,674 --> 00:13:43,833
Was there anybody, who was against the Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

181
00:13:44,181 --> 00:13:45,079
قال سعيد: لا

182
00:13:45,169 --> 00:13:45,470
No!

183
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:47,669
لم يخالفه إلَّا مرتد

184
00:13:48,493 --> 00:13:52,328
No one would go against Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and refuse to give him Baiyah(بَيْعة) except a Murtadd(مرتد)

185
00:13:52,882 --> 00:13:53,859
أوكاد أن يرتد

186
00:13:53,884 --> 00:13:56,445
Or somebody, who is about to become a Murtad(مرتد)

187
00:13:56,895 --> 00:13:58,326
وقد أنقضى الله أنصار

188
00:13:58,351 --> 00:14:00,478
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ saved the Ansaar(أنْصَار)

189
00:14:00,662 --> 00:14:02,293
فجمعهم عليه وَ اَبايعهم

190
00:14:02,695 --> 00:14:06,403
Allah saved the Ansaar(أنْصَار) and protected them, and made them all give him Baiyah(بَيْعة).

191
00:14:06,474 --> 00:14:09,530
Because we talked about what happened with Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار).

192
00:14:09,878 --> 00:14:11,331
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ saved them

193
00:14:12,170 --> 00:14:15,503
and made them give Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

194
00:14:15,858 --> 00:14:16,465
And then he said:

195
00:14:16,687 --> 00:14:19,134
هل قاعدة أحدٌ من المهاجرين عن بيعتِ؟

196
00:14:19,474 --> 00:14:23,519
Was there anybody from among the Muhajireen(مهاجرين), who did not give him Baiyah(بَيْعة).

197
00:14:23,749 --> 00:14:24,923
 He responded by saying;

198
00:14:24,963 --> 00:14:27,617
لأ لقد تتابع على مهاجرون على بيعة

199
00:14:27,641 --> 00:14:30,202
No! All of them came and gave him Baiyah(بَيْعة).

200
00:14:31,730 --> 00:14:33,699
so it is a very clear issue.

201
00:14:34,438 --> 00:14:38,632
A second issue that is brought up is the issue of inheritance.

202
00:14:39,949 --> 00:14:44,212
Fatimah رضي الله عنها and Al-Abbas(العباس), the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

203
00:14:44,536 --> 00:14:52,024
went to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, asking for their inheritance from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

204
00:14:53,591 --> 00:14:55,486
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

205
00:14:56,420 --> 00:15:01,194
I've heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say about the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء)

206
00:15:01,250 --> 00:15:03,687
لا نورث ما تركنا صدقه

207
00:15:04,433 --> 00:15:08,267
The Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah are not inherited - What they leave, is Sadaqah(صدقه).

208
00:15:09,384 --> 00:15:14,538
The Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah, they are excluded from the laws of inheritance.

209
00:15:14,839 --> 00:15:18,206
The Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ do not leave behind any inheritance

210
00:15:18,757 --> 00:15:24,213
the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah - the Nabi(نَبِي) is the father of his Ummah(امة)

211
00:15:25,311 --> 00:15:27,207
the Nabi(نَبِي) is the father of his Ummah(امة).

212
00:15:27,857 --> 00:15:29,826
What do we call the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ?

213
00:15:30,359 --> 00:15:33,722
Ummahat-Ul Mo'mineen(أمهات المؤمنين), the Mothers of the Believers.

214
00:15:34,265 --> 00:15:36,169
And what was the Ibrahim عليه السّلام called,

215
00:15:36,923 --> 00:15:40,044
اباک ابراھیم هو سماک المسلمين من قبل وفي هذا

216
00:15:40,587 --> 00:15:44,373
That he is your father Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and He is the one, who named you Muslims.

217
00:15:44,744 --> 00:15:46,745
He is the one, who gave us this name of Muslims.

218
00:15:47,874 --> 00:15:50,578
So the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), they do not leave behind inheritance.

219
00:15:51,239 --> 00:15:55,682
So when Fatima(فاطمه) and Al-Abbas(العباس) came to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) they did not know this Hadith(حديث).

220
00:15:55,984 --> 00:15:59,897
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه told them about it and they accepted that

221
00:16:00,387 --> 00:16:02,856
So they did not received the inheritance.

222
00:16:03,197 --> 00:16:04,742
And then Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said;

223
00:16:05,098 --> 00:16:09,417
لست تاركً شيئًا كان رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يعمل به إلَّا عملتُ به

224
00:16:09,656 --> 00:16:12,087
فإنِّي أخش إن تركت شيعًا من أمره أنظير

225
00:16:12,411 --> 00:16:15,934
And I'm not going to disobey any order, of the orders of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

226
00:16:16,164 --> 00:16:19,067
and I'm going to follow his way because if I don't, I'm going to go astray.

227
00:16:21,595 --> 00:16:23,030
Al-Qadhi Ayyaz(ألقاضي أياز), he says;

228
00:16:23,409 --> 00:16:28,461
وفي تركي فاطمه منازعت أبي بكرٍ بعد إحتجاجه عليها بالحديث

229
00:16:29,044 --> 00:16:35,744
ألتسليم لالعجماع على قضية وانَّها لمَّا بلغها الحديث وبين لها تعويل تركت رائها

230
00:16:35,768 --> 00:16:41,265
ثم لم يكن منها ولا منزريتها بعد ذالك طلبٌ ميراث

231
00:16:41,472 --> 00:16:46,346
 ثم وليَّ عليٌ خلافه فلم يعدل بها عمَّا فعله ابوبكرو عمر رضي الله عنه

232
00:16:46,656 --> 00:16:47,688
Al-Qadhi Ayyaz(ألقاضي أياز) says,

233
00:16:47,902 --> 00:16:53,779
 that when Fatimah رضي الله عنها heard that from Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), she had no hard feelings at all, and she accepted it.

234
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:57,621
And even when Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) became the Khalifah(خليفه) later on,

235
00:16:57,750 --> 00:16:59,428
he did not change what Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) did.

236
00:17:00,362 --> 00:17:04,957
So even Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه, who's part of the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ

237
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:08,437
did not change the way of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه,

238
00:17:08,574 --> 00:17:12,995
regarding the inheritance of Rasul Ullah صلوات الله والسلام عليه.

239
00:17:13,874 --> 00:17:18,699
We move on to the next topic, and that is the army of Usamah(أسامه).

240
00:17:20,531 --> 00:17:23,746
After three days of the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ

241
00:17:24,625 --> 00:17:27,687
and the appointment of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) as Khalifah(خليفه),

242
00:17:28,175 --> 00:17:29,424
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said;

243
00:17:29,623 --> 00:17:38,892
لِيُتِمَّا بعث أسامة على لا يبقين فى المدينة أحدٌ من جندٍي أسامه إلَّا خرج إلى أستره بالجرف

244
00:17:40,115 --> 00:17:44,067
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said the army of Usamah(أسامة) should go out.

245
00:17:44,602 --> 00:17:48,076
No one from the army of Usamah(أسامة) should stay in Madina

246
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:50,885
and they should go to the camp in Al-Jurf(ألجرف).

247
00:17:52,764 --> 00:17:56,478
A little bit of background, in the eighth year of Hijrah(هجرة),

248
00:17:56,502 --> 00:18:06,023
Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed an army to go, for the first time ever, and face the Romans

249
00:18:08,644 --> 00:18:15,890
and Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed his beloved Zaid Bin Harissah رضي الله عنه to lead that army.

250
00:18:17,217 --> 00:18:21,994
Second in command was Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر إبن أبي طالب), his cousin.

251
00:18:23,130 --> 00:18:26,999
Third in command is Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة), one among the Ansaar(أنْصَار).

252
00:18:28,308 --> 00:18:32,230
The army was 3000, and they were to go out to Ash-Sham(ألشام).

253
00:18:34,023 --> 00:18:37,166
This was the first time ever the Muslims are going to meet the Romans.

254
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:48,953
So this army marches out and to their surprise they see in front of them an enemy that is filling the horizon

255
00:18:49,964 --> 00:18:52,086
as far as you can see, soldiers.

256
00:18:53,145 --> 00:18:57,530
They were 3000, while the enemy was 200,000.

257
00:18:59,503 --> 00:19:03,373
As-Sahabah رضي الله عنهم never ever saw a crowd like that in their life

258
00:19:04,081 --> 00:19:09,998
you know, in the, in Arabia, you don't have such a population to start with to have an army of 200,000.

259
00:19:10,923 --> 00:19:14,049
Arabia was scarcely populated tribes were small

260
00:19:14,772 --> 00:19:16,424
you didn't have these huge numbers.

261
00:19:17,107 --> 00:19:23,314
So the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم are now seeing an army of 200,000 something that they never saw before

262
00:19:24,377 --> 00:19:25,713
and they were only 3000,

263
00:19:27,074 --> 00:19:28,743
so they go back to make Shura(شورى).

264
00:19:29,946 --> 00:19:36,813
Some of them say this army is so huge in numbers that we are excused to go back

265
00:19:36,876 --> 00:19:40,777
and we know that in Qur'an it says that, if you are strong than one can face 10

266
00:19:41,374 --> 00:19:43,921
if you're weak then one faces two.

267
00:19:45,868 --> 00:19:48,654
So they have an excuse, they have the right to go back.

268
00:19:49,322 --> 00:19:51,737
But Abdullah Bin Rawaha رضي الله عنه, he said;

269
00:19:53,626 --> 00:19:57,934
We have came here for Shahadah(شهادة), so why should we go back,

270
00:19:58,227 --> 00:20:01,184
if that's what we came here for, Why should we retreat.?

271
00:20:01,579 --> 00:20:05,694
If we are searching for Shahadah(شهادة), then why do we go back.

272
00:20:06,441 --> 00:20:07,973
So they decided to go ahead.

273
00:20:08,616 --> 00:20:11,118
They fought the first day, the second day, the third day.

274
00:20:12,468 --> 00:20:14,722
Zaid Bin Harissa رضي الله عنه was killed.

275
00:20:15,047 --> 00:20:16,452
So who took over?

276
00:20:17,166 --> 00:20:18,142
Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر إبن أبي طالب)

277
00:20:18,219 --> 00:20:20,021
and we talked about this and then he was killed

278
00:20:20,124 --> 00:20:21,751
and then Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) was killed.

279
00:20:21,895 --> 00:20:25,138
The three of them were killed, and then Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) took over,

280
00:20:25,432 --> 00:20:29,068
 and he made a successful retreat with the army.

281
00:20:30,439 --> 00:20:34,632
The next year Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to go out himself

282
00:20:36,230 --> 00:20:40,522
So, he prepared the army for Ghazwat Tabook(غزوة التبوك).

283
00:20:43,290 --> 00:20:46,208
They went out and the Romans did not dare to come and faced them.

284
00:20:46,697 --> 00:20:51,859
So there was no fighting that occurred and Rasool Allah ﷺ went back without being harmed

285
00:20:52,803 --> 00:20:53,899
 and no fighting occurred.

286
00:20:54,473 --> 00:21:00,487
The third year Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to send out Usama Bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد) to lead an army

287
00:21:00,654 --> 00:21:04,931
 and he told him, I want you, to go and step over with your horses

288
00:21:05,409 --> 00:21:07,774
the same place where your father was killed.

289
00:21:09,168 --> 00:21:12,110
So Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed Usama Bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد) to lead an army

290
00:21:12,134 --> 00:21:17,099
and to go and fight and to pass over the same place where Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) was killed.

291
00:21:18,571 --> 00:21:21,019
A few days after that, Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

292
00:21:22,266 --> 00:21:26,649
So now for three years Rasool Allah ﷺ is arranging a campaign

293
00:21:27,200 --> 00:21:29,226
to conquer the Roman Empire.

294
00:21:30,519 --> 00:21:34,957
Mu'ta(موته), Tabook(تبوك) and then the third year, the army of Usama Bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد).

295
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:43,154
The way they used to gather the army because they didn't have uniform soldiers there wasn't a professional army

296
00:21:43,313 --> 00:21:48,014
I mean, everyone among the Sahabah(صحابه) was expected to participate in Jihad(جهاد).

297
00:21:49,377 --> 00:21:50,631
So the way they would do it, is

298
00:21:50,655 --> 00:21:53,524
they would have their campgrounds, outside of Madina

299
00:21:53,848 --> 00:21:59,219
and then the soldiers would flood into that campground until the army is ready to go, then it would leave.

300
00:22:00,087 --> 00:22:02,014
So this campground was Al-Jurf(ألجرف).

301
00:22:02,338 --> 00:22:05,254
Rasool Allah ﷺ told the army to go and camp in Al-Jurf(ألجرف).

302
00:22:05,798 --> 00:22:08,578
Some people they could get ready an hour, some people days

303
00:22:08,769 --> 00:22:10,979
So the Army has to be outside of Madina.

304
00:22:12,014 --> 00:22:15,309
So, that the Ameer(أمير) of the army would know how many soldiers are there

305
00:22:15,333 --> 00:22:18,920
and they need to be separated from the residents in Madina.

306
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:24,927
When Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away, all of those soldiers, who were in Al-Jurf(ألجرف) they came back to Madina.

307
00:22:25,760 --> 00:22:30,508
Three days later, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is telling them to go back.

308
00:22:33,476 --> 00:22:36,271
Usama Bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد), he obeys the order and he goes out to Al-Jurf(ألجرف)

309
00:22:36,295 --> 00:22:37,801
and some of the soldiers go with him.

310
00:22:37,872 --> 00:22:40,356
But now the Sahabah رضي الله عنه are coming to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

311
00:22:41,040 --> 00:22:45,664
and try to imagine the situation, it's just three days after Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

312
00:22:46,238 --> 00:22:50,651
I mean, they're still going through the pain and agony of the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

313
00:22:50,722 --> 00:22:52,229
 they're preoccupied with that

314
00:22:52,499 --> 00:22:57,425
and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is telling them to go out and to fight the Romans.

315
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:01,423
So they came to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

316
00:23:01,537 --> 00:23:06,273
and Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), he narrates this, he says that they told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

317
00:23:06,457 --> 00:23:11,709
إن هؤلاء جل المسلمين، والعرب على ما ترى قد انتقضت بك

318
00:23:12,026 --> 00:23:15,487
فليس ينبغي لك أن تفرق عنك جماعة المسلمين

319
00:23:16,635 --> 00:23:20,333
They said: This army is the majority of the Muslims

320
00:23:20,923 --> 00:23:24,861
and the Arabs have cut their ties with you.

321
00:23:26,396 --> 00:23:33,012
So we don't think that it is appropriate for you to disperse the Jama'ah(جماعة) of the Muslims.

322
00:23:33,815 --> 00:23:37,633
This army is the Jama'ah(جماعة) of the Muslimeen(مسلمين) and now you're going to send them out.

323
00:23:38,294 --> 00:23:41,614
While all of the Arabs around us, are thinking about attacking us.

324
00:23:43,392 --> 00:23:46,450
And these deliberations were going on

325
00:23:46,837 --> 00:23:49,559
they again tried to convince the Khalifah(خليفه)

326
00:23:49,583 --> 00:23:53,733
 and the most outspoken person among them was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

327
00:23:54,214 --> 00:23:56,210
He told Al-Khalifah(ألخليفه)

328
00:23:57,105 --> 00:23:57,904
إن معي

329
00:23:58,190 --> 00:24:00,340
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was here

330
00:24:00,532 --> 00:24:02,430
carrying a message from Usama bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد)

331
00:24:02,454 --> 00:24:03,772
because Usama bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد) wasn't present.

332
00:24:03,796 --> 00:24:05,256
Usama bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد) was in Al-Jurf(ألجرف).

333
00:24:05,767 --> 00:24:08,821
So Usama(أسامه) told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to go to the Khalifah(خليفه)

334
00:24:08,845 --> 00:24:11,106
and convey my message to him. He said;

335
00:24:11,236 --> 00:24:17,711
إن معي وجوه المسلمين وجلتهم ولا آمن على خليفة رسول الله

336
00:24:18,005 --> 00:24:22,170
وحرم رسول الله والمسلمين أن يتخطفهم المشركون

337
00:24:23,788 --> 00:24:29,793
I have with me, the leadership of the Muslims and the majority of their men.

338
00:24:30,551 --> 00:24:33,918
And I don't feel safe on the Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

339
00:24:34,328 --> 00:24:38,088
and the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ, from the Mushrikeen(مشركين).

340
00:24:38,318 --> 00:24:39,633
Usama bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد) is saying

341
00:24:39,697 --> 00:24:44,533
 this army of mine has the leadership of the community, and it has the fighters

342
00:24:45,748 --> 00:24:49,673
and I am worried that the Mushrikeen(مشركين) will come and snatch away the Khalifah(خليفه),

343
00:24:50,085 --> 00:24:51,816
 and the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

344
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:59,473
Now, the Sahabah(صحابه) are feeling the weight of the responsibility of protecting the household of Rasool Ullah.

345
00:25:01,109 --> 00:25:07,982
After Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away, it's the responsibility of the Sahabah(صحابه), to protect his wives, to protect his family.

346
00:25:08,689 --> 00:25:13,751
So, Usama bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد) is saying that our priority and this was also the opinion of all of the Sahabah(صحابه)

347
00:25:14,041 --> 00:25:16,525
our priority now is to protect the Khalifah(خليفه)

348
00:25:16,928 --> 00:25:19,211
and to protect the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

349
00:25:19,465 --> 00:25:22,763
and to protect the town of Islam, the city of Islam - Madina.

350
00:25:22,877 --> 00:25:26,817
Because all around us, there's a movement of Riddah(ردة)

351
00:25:27,631 --> 00:25:31,595
the base of the Muslims is Madina, and that's where the army should stay.

352
00:25:32,334 --> 00:25:34,620
And it's a very valid point and it makes sense.

353
00:25:35,249 --> 00:25:39,791
Why should our priority now be to fight the Roman Empire,

354
00:25:40,389 --> 00:25:43,917
who are not an eminent danger at this particular moment

355
00:25:44,249 --> 00:25:49,304
 and leave Madina, that could be ambushed at any moment of the night or day.

356
00:25:50,492 --> 00:25:55,558
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه after hearing all of the different views.

357
00:25:56,073 --> 00:25:59,658
And after being pressured by the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم especially Umar(عُمَر)

358
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:06,676
even the leader of the army who's sending out, Usama bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد) doesn't think he should go out.

359
00:26:07,676 --> 00:26:10,710
 Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he gathers all the Muslims in the Masjid(مسجد)

360
00:26:10,757 --> 00:26:15,457
 and he stands up and he delivers the following very brief speech, he says;

361
00:26:16,261 --> 00:26:24,606
والذي نفس أبي بكر بيده، لو ظننت أن السباع تخطفني لأنفذت بعث أسامة

362
00:26:24,993 --> 00:26:31,616
كما أمر به رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم، ولو لم يبق في القرى غيري لأنفذته

363
00:26:32,846 --> 00:26:36,151
By Him, in Whose hands is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)'s soul.

364
00:26:36,906 --> 00:26:40,941
Even if I thought that the beasts of prey would snatch me away

365
00:26:41,202 --> 00:26:44,189
I would carry out the sending of the army of Usama(أسامة)

366
00:26:44,434 --> 00:26:46,686
just as the messenger of Allah ordered.

367
00:26:47,346 --> 00:26:51,622
Even if there remained in the villages, no one but myself, I would carry it out.

368
00:26:52,900 --> 00:26:56,156
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is putting an end to all of the arguments,

369
00:26:56,273 --> 00:27:00,069
he's saying, not only if they take over Madina

370
00:27:00,442 --> 00:27:04,530
if they succeed in destroying the whole community

371
00:27:04,562 --> 00:27:08,116
and no one remains but me I'm the only person left

372
00:27:08,362 --> 00:27:10,112
I'm still gonna send this army out.

373
00:27:12,836 --> 00:27:16,312
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is not here talking about strategy

374
00:27:16,779 --> 00:27:20,040
he is not talking about what is the most beneficial.

375
00:27:20,945 --> 00:27:24,202
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) is talking about what is the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Ullah,

376
00:27:24,242 --> 00:27:25,776
 what is following the messenger of Allah

377
00:27:26,561 --> 00:27:29,577
إِنَّمَا أَنَا مُتَّبِعٌ وَلَسْتُ بِمُبْتَدِعٍ،

378
00:27:30,217 --> 00:27:34,429
I am a follower of the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, and I am not an innovator

379
00:27:35,449 --> 00:27:39,274
 he was making it clear that his method of government,

380
00:27:39,695 --> 00:27:44,758
 his policy will be to follow the footsteps of Rasool Allah ﷺ no matter what.

381
00:27:45,465 --> 00:27:49,082
Even if that means that the whole community will be destroyed

382
00:27:49,352 --> 00:27:51,808
I'm still going to follow the way of Rasool Ullah

383
00:27:52,250 --> 00:27:55,137
even if I'm the only person to be left behind

384
00:27:56,539 --> 00:28:00,288
and this is an extremely difficult position to take.

385
00:28:01,386 --> 00:28:06,298
And you need to think about the mindset of the Sahabah(صحابه) at that particular time,

386
00:28:06,338 --> 00:28:07,767
 Rasool Allah ﷺ just passed away

387
00:28:07,957 --> 00:28:12,218
 and Ayesha رضي الله عنها, I mean look at the description of Ayesha(عائشه) of the situations.

388
00:28:12,258 --> 00:28:12,820
 She says:

389
00:28:12,910 --> 00:28:16,365
لما قبض رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم ارتدت العرب قاطبة !

390
00:28:16,785 --> 00:28:22,162
واشرأب النفاق والله قد نزل بي ما لو نزل بالجبال الرَّاسيات لهادها

391
00:28:22,710 --> 00:28:25,956
وصار أصحاب محمَّد كأنَّهم مِعْزَى مطيرة

392
00:28:26,101 --> 00:28:29,295
في حشٍّ في ليلةٍ مطيرةٍ بأرض مسبعةٍ

393
00:28:29,923 --> 00:28:31,204
Ayesha رضي الله عنها said;

394
00:28:31,500 --> 00:28:35,665
When Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away all of the Arabs apostated

395
00:28:36,639 --> 00:28:40,617
and the necks of the Munafiqeen(منافقين) started sticking up.

396
00:28:41,228 --> 00:28:47,824
In the Name of Allah, my father was carrying a burden if it was placed over mountains, it would destroy them.

397
00:28:49,375 --> 00:28:55,764
And the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ became like scattered goats in the stormy cold night,

398
00:28:56,202 --> 00:28:59,284
  which is an inland that is filled with wolves.

399
00:29:00,101 --> 00:29:03,511
She said, that the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Ullah, became like scattered goats

400
00:29:03,645 --> 00:29:05,102
because the Shepherd has passed away.

401
00:29:05,672 --> 00:29:13,399
They were like scattered goats in rainy night, very dark, and the whole area is infested with wolves.

402
00:29:14,468 --> 00:29:18,128
That is the description of Ayesha رضي الله عنها to the situation of the Sahabah(صحابه)

403
00:29:18,504 --> 00:29:22,403
 there was fear, there was difficulty, there were enemies from every direction

404
00:29:22,650 --> 00:29:25,033
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is saying: I don't care about that.

405
00:29:25,936 --> 00:29:28,988
I'm going to follow the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ and you're gonna have to follow me.

406
00:29:29,867 --> 00:29:31,667
Ibn Hajar Al-Asqalani(إبن حجر ألعسقلاني), he says,

407
00:29:31,920 --> 00:29:37,598
the position of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) shows that not all the time the majority opinion is right.

408
00:29:38,071 --> 00:29:41,294
 Sometimes, a lone person could have the right opinion

409
00:29:41,916 --> 00:29:46,489
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was going against the majority of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

410
00:29:46,689 --> 00:29:47,820
but he was right.

411
00:29:48,830 --> 00:29:54,854
Like Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) says that he had the best opinion among all of the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

412
00:29:56,054 --> 00:30:00,173
because of the time that he spent with Rasool Allah ﷺ

413
00:30:00,497 --> 00:30:03,106
and drinking from the fountain of the Prophet-hood as I mentioned to you

414
00:30:06,734 --> 00:30:08,464
and this is a position of Yaqeen(يقين).

415
00:30:09,054 --> 00:30:12,744
You can't take that position taking that stance, unless you have Yaqeen(يقين).

416
00:30:13,646 --> 00:30:16,573
I mean this is something that is not based on intelligence,

417
00:30:16,641 --> 00:30:18,995
and this is something that is based on Eeman(ايمان).

418
00:30:19,450 --> 00:30:21,233
How deep your faith is.

419
00:30:21,983 --> 00:30:24,732
 Similar to like the situation of Musa عليه السّلام,

420
00:30:24,951 --> 00:30:28,750
when the sea was in front of him, and the army of Firaun(فرعون) was behind him.

421
00:30:30,086 --> 00:30:34,082
He has told Bannu Israel(بنو اسرائيل), that Allah will give us victory Allah will save us.

422
00:30:34,435 --> 00:30:38,692
 But now the real world is telling you, otherwise.

423
00:30:39,139 --> 00:30:43,549
Your eyes are telling you that the army is behind me, and the sea is in front of me

424
00:30:44,067 --> 00:30:47,580
and your ears are hearing nothing but the complaints of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل)

425
00:30:48,083 --> 00:30:51,774
you lie to us, you promise us that we will be saved

426
00:30:51,805 --> 00:30:54,332
and the army of Firaun(فرعون) is right behind us.

427
00:30:54,356 --> 00:30:57,198
And you get affected by the opinion of the people around you

428
00:30:57,222 --> 00:31:00,178
especially when you're hearing the same thing again and again,

429
00:31:00,698 --> 00:31:03,331
 just like the information minister of Hitler.

430
00:31:03,355 --> 00:31:05,579
He said: We're going to keep on lying, until people believe it.

431
00:31:06,365 --> 00:31:09,050
You keep on repeating the lie and people in the end will buy it.

432
00:31:10,719 --> 00:31:14,264
But Musa عليه السّلام due to his Yaqeen(يقين), he said;

433
00:31:14,288 --> 00:31:16,873
كَلا إِنَّ مَعِيَ رَبِّي سَيَهْدِينِ

434
00:31:16,978 --> 00:31:19,014
 No! Allah is with me and He will guide me.

435
00:31:20,213 --> 00:31:22,605
I don't believe my eyes, I don't believe my ears.

436
00:31:23,218 --> 00:31:28,124
Allah has promised me and it will happen and it was a test from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

437
00:31:28,148 --> 00:31:31,433
and Allah then told him to split the sea with your stick and Allah saved them.

438
00:31:32,149 --> 00:31:36,276
Or like Rasool Allah ﷺ, when somebody came to him complaining that his brother is sick.

439
00:31:36,471 --> 00:31:38,512
 Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Give him honey!

440
00:31:39,688 --> 00:31:42,802
He later on came and said he wasn't cured.

441
00:31:42,845 --> 00:31:44,265
Rasool Ullah said: Give him honey!

442
00:31:44,611 --> 00:31:47,987
Again, he came back a third time, said: My brother isn't cured.

443
00:31:48,095 --> 00:31:49,307
He said: Give him honey.

444
00:31:49,869 --> 00:31:53,602
The fourth time he said, he came back and said my brother wasn't cured.

445
00:31:54,028 --> 00:31:56,873
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, Allah is telling the truth

446
00:31:56,983 --> 00:31:58,914
and the stomach of your brother is lying.

447
00:32:00,711 --> 00:32:02,134
Allah is telling the truth.

448
00:32:02,286 --> 00:32:03,647
What Allah says is the truth.

449
00:32:03,759 --> 00:32:07,607
Allah has described the honey as being Shifa(شفاء), it is Shifa(شفاء).

450
00:32:08,650 --> 00:32:10,302
The stomach of your brother is lying.

451
00:32:12,681 --> 00:32:14,659
Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبن ألقيم), he explains this Hadith(حديث), he says:

452
00:32:14,684 --> 00:32:19,039
The problem here is that he didn't give his brother, the sufficient dose, of the medicine

453
00:32:19,674 --> 00:32:20,727
he didn't give him enough.

454
00:32:22,372 --> 00:32:27,095
So you have Yaqeen(يقين) in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and you believe in what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ promised.

455
00:32:27,661 --> 00:32:29,708
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was saying that

456
00:32:29,732 --> 00:32:32,060
I am going to follow the way of Rasool Ullah.

457
00:32:33,072 --> 00:32:37,958
Keep in mind that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) here is setting the ground rules of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

458
00:32:38,868 --> 00:32:41,780
The Khalifah(خليفه) must follow the footsteps of the Nabi(نَبِي)

459
00:32:42,980 --> 00:32:45,263
إِنَّمَا أَنَا مُتَّبِعٌ وَلَسْتُ بِمُبْتَدِعٍ،

460
00:32:45,806 --> 00:32:48,601
I am a follower and I'm not an innovator.

461
00:32:48,969 --> 00:32:55,077
When that happened, the Ansaar(أنْصَار) they told Umar(عُمَر) to go back and tell the Khalifah(خليفه) that

462
00:32:55,886 --> 00:32:58,580
if he's not going to agree to keep the army

463
00:32:59,186 --> 00:33:01,030
then at least have him appoint somebody who's older.

464
00:33:02,011 --> 00:33:06,947
 Usama Bin Zaid(أسامة بن زيد) is 18 years old, and the situation is very difficult, now.

465
00:33:07,048 --> 00:33:11,723
We want to have somebody who has more maturity and more wisdom somebody who's older.

466
00:33:12,091 --> 00:33:15,951
 Now, that there was already some talk going on about the Imraa(إمراء) of Usama(أسامة) before that

467
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:17,431
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

468
00:33:18,579 --> 00:33:22,962
If you are talking about the leadership of Usama(أسامة).

469
00:33:23,905 --> 00:33:26,700
You've also said the same about his father before.

470
00:33:27,821 --> 00:33:31,343
And his father was befitting for that position

471
00:33:33,269 --> 00:33:35,568
and I love his father, and I loved his son.

472
00:33:37,057 --> 00:33:40,197
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and said;

473
00:33:40,795 --> 00:33:43,719
Would you consider appointing somebody, who is older in age.

474
00:33:44,622 --> 00:33:48,936
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه sprung up angrily and said;

475
00:33:48,967 --> 00:33:57,072
ثكلتك أمك وعدمتك يا ابن الخطاب، استعمله رسول الله وتأمرني أن أنزِعَه

476
00:33:58,786 --> 00:34:00,389
At this Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) sprang up and he said;

477
00:34:00,477 --> 00:34:04,760
May your mother be bereft of you and destitute of you, Ibn Al-Khattab(إبن ألخطاب),

478
00:34:04,943 --> 00:34:08,819
the Messenger of Allah appointed him and you order me to dismiss him.

479
00:34:09,941 --> 00:34:12,978
Rasool Allah ﷺ is the one, who appointed Usama(أسامة), you want me to change him.

480
00:34:13,435 --> 00:34:15,129
So he refused to change Usama(أسامة),

481
00:34:15,270 --> 00:34:19,194
and he refused to change any of his Umara'a(أمراء) after that, as we mentioned before.

482
00:34:19,767 --> 00:34:26,868
So now, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه after the army was all camped in Al-Jurf(ألجرف)  and is ready to set out

483
00:34:27,797 --> 00:34:32,295
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was on his camel

484
00:34:32,776 --> 00:34:37,761
and his camel was being led by Abdur Rahman Ibn auf رضي الله عنه.

485
00:34:37,785 --> 00:34:42,376
So they went out to, which is called Tashiee Al-Jaish(تشيع ألجيش)

486
00:34:43,130 --> 00:34:44,364
escorting the army.

487
00:34:45,310 --> 00:34:48,994
Rasool Allah ﷺ would do that he would walk with the Army, until it leaves

488
00:34:49,475 --> 00:34:51,561
and then he would give them his farewell.

489
00:34:52,151 --> 00:34:53,656
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is following the same Sunnah(سنة).

490
00:34:54,768 --> 00:35:00,759
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is walking and Usama Bin Zaid(أسامة بن زيد) the 18 year old is riding over his camel.

491
00:35:02,554 --> 00:35:05,952
And you know, out of respect, you come down your camel

492
00:35:05,976 --> 00:35:08,712
and you have the older person, ride the camel.

493
00:35:08,736 --> 00:35:14,176
ليس منا من لم يعقر كبيرنا ويعطف على صغيرنا

494
00:35:14,977 --> 00:35:18,750
The one, who does not give respect to the elderly among us does not belong to us

495
00:35:19,168 --> 00:35:23,111
and the one, who does not have mercy on our children, does not belong to us.

496
00:35:24,203 --> 00:35:27,700
So Usama Bin Zaid(أسامة بن زيد) wants to come down from his camel

497
00:35:27,899 --> 00:35:32,483
and he's telling Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), I'm going to come down and you ride the camel.

498
00:35:33,369 --> 00:35:40,217
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: I want my feet to get dirty walking in the path of Allah.

499
00:35:42,479 --> 00:35:44,697
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ says that

500
00:35:45,296 --> 00:35:54,803
a person whose feet are dirty, in walking in the path of Allah, Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) will be saved from hellfire.

501
00:35:56,011 --> 00:36:03,017
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه wants to walk on the sand on the dirt and get his feet dirty

502
00:36:03,333 --> 00:36:07,209
so that he will at least have a few steps in the path of Allah.

503
00:36:07,233 --> 00:36:10,693
If he's not going to go out with the army, at least he'll have a few steps.

504
00:36:12,049 --> 00:36:16,704
And then he delivered a Khut'ba(خطبة), to the army, and

505
00:36:17,138 --> 00:36:25,440
this is like the Muslim constitution when it comes to warfare the rules and regulations of war in Islam.

506
00:36:27,375 --> 00:36:33,879
لا تخونُوا، ولا تَغُلُّوا،ولا تغدرو، ولا تُمثِّلوا، ولا تقتُلُوا طفلاً صغيراً،

507
00:36:34,039 --> 00:36:40,325
ولا شيخاً ، ولا امرأة، ولا تَعْقِروا نخلاً ولا تُحْرِقُوه، ولا تَقْطَعوا شَجَرَةً مُثْمِرَةً،

508
00:36:40,607 --> 00:36:44,332
ولا تَذْبَحُوا شاةً ولا بقرةً ولا بعيراً إلا لَمأكَلَةٍ

509
00:36:44,965 --> 00:36:48,658
وسوفَ تمرُّونَ بأقوامٍ قد فرَّغُوا أنفسَهم في الصَّوامعِ

510
00:36:49,038 --> 00:36:51,595
فدعوهمْ وما فرّغُوا أنفسَهم له

511
00:36:52,042 --> 00:36:59,791
وسوف تَقْدَمُون على قومٍ يأتونكم بآنيةٍ فيها ألوانُ الطعامِ، فإذا أكلْتُمْ منها شيئاً فاذكُروا اسمَ اللهِ عليها

512
00:37:02,105 --> 00:37:08,316
O army, stop, and I will order you 10 things, learn them from me by heart.

513
00:37:09,070 --> 00:37:11,209
You shall not engage in treachery,

514
00:37:11,714 --> 00:37:13,626
You shall not steal from the booty.

515
00:37:14,265 --> 00:37:16,162
 You shall not act unfaithfully,

516
00:37:16,505 --> 00:37:18,395
You shall not engage in deception.

517
00:37:19,180 --> 00:37:21,174
You should not indulge in mutilation,

518
00:37:21,527 --> 00:37:26,142
you shall kill neither young child, nor an old man nor a woman.

519
00:37:26,554 --> 00:37:29,071
You shall not fell palm trees or burn them.

520
00:37:29,615 --> 00:37:32,169
You shall not cut down any fruit bearing tree.

521
00:37:32,697 --> 00:37:36,902
You shall not slaughter a sheep or a cow or a camel, except for food.

522
00:37:37,656 --> 00:37:42,622
You will pass by people who occupy themselves in monasteries

523
00:37:43,063 --> 00:37:47,619
 leave them alone and leave them alone with what they have busy themselves with.

524
00:37:48,123 --> 00:37:52,159
You will come to our people who will bring you vessels in which are varieties of food.

525
00:37:52,672 --> 00:37:57,089
If you eat anything from these dishes mentioned the name of ALLAH over them.

526
00:37:58,766 --> 00:38:03,344
These were the words of advice that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) gave to his armies.

527
00:38:05,856 --> 00:38:09,006
There are a few statements here that I'm going to note

528
00:38:10,806 --> 00:38:11,794
