733
00:52:22,204 --> 00:52:25,991
because they just completely dismantle their plans of attacking Madina.

734
00:52:26,807 --> 00:52:35,091
Now, Heracul(هرقل), the Roman emperor was so worried about this new phenomenon of Islam.

735
00:52:35,474 --> 00:52:36,658
 He left his capital

736
00:52:37,545 --> 00:52:43,932
and he set base in Antakia(أنتاكيه), Antioch in Syria, in present day Syria.

737
00:52:44,358 --> 00:52:49,397
Because he wanted to be close to the events that were occurring in this forgotten land of Arabia.

738
00:52:49,430 --> 00:52:50,749
I mean nothing was happening there.

739
00:52:51,643 --> 00:52:56,774
Armies would cross back and forth, and they wouldn't even take a glimpse at the desert.

740
00:52:57,542 --> 00:53:00,846
There's no resources there, there's scarcely any people there

741
00:53:01,223 --> 00:53:02,984
what would you want with such a wasteland.?

742
00:53:03,450 --> 00:53:05,441
So the Persian Empire at the height of its power

743
00:53:05,466 --> 00:53:08,979
and the Roman Empire at the height of his power never thought about invading Arabia.

744
00:53:09,020 --> 00:53:12,187
What are you going to do with this desolate land as they viewed it.

745
00:53:13,167 --> 00:53:18,415
And now, the Roman Emperor leaves his capital and goes to Antakia(أنتاكيه)

746
00:53:18,569 --> 00:53:21,361
just to monitor events in Madina.

747
00:53:22,253 --> 00:53:25,688
He's so worried about it, that he moves from his capital.

748
00:53:27,564 --> 00:53:30,476
The Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah is that, he would receive the news

749
00:53:30,971 --> 00:53:33,672
of the army of Usama(أسامه) attacking him

750
00:53:33,786 --> 00:53:35,874
and the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ the same day.

751
00:53:36,519 --> 00:53:38,297
Heracul(هرقل) said: What's going on?

752
00:53:39,094 --> 00:53:42,109
Their prophet, their leader just passed away

753
00:53:42,358 --> 00:53:44,585
and they're sending out an army to fight me.

754
00:53:45,855 --> 00:53:52,879
So he changed his mind and he allowed the army of Usama(أسامه) to make it into the depth of the Roman Empire,

755
00:53:53,507 --> 00:53:56,968
 to take booty and to leave unharmed.

756
00:53:57,785 --> 00:54:03,884
Usama Bin Zaid(أسامة بن زيد) marches with his horses over the land in which his father was killed,

757
00:54:04,275 --> 00:54:07,914
 he makes negotiations and deals with the Arab tribes in the area.

758
00:54:08,274 --> 00:54:10,788
 He signs agreements and truces with them.

759
00:54:11,253 --> 00:54:15,239
He takes Jizya(جزية), he takes booty of war and goes back

760
00:54:15,531 --> 00:54:18,960
and Heracul(هرقل) is right there, he did not dare to send out an army to meet him.

761
00:54:20,197 --> 00:54:23,592
These were the results of the Yaqeen(يقين) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

762
00:54:25,635 --> 00:54:27,192
this is what happens when you have Yaqeen(يقين).

763
00:54:27,711 --> 00:54:33,420
The mother of Musa عليه السّلام, if she did not have Yaqeen(يقين) in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

764
00:54:34,225 --> 00:54:37,984
and rather than throwing her child in the river which seems as definite death,

765
00:54:38,460 --> 00:54:39,593
 because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ told her

766
00:54:39,719 --> 00:54:42,856
if you fear on the safety of your child, do what? Throw him in the river.

767
00:54:43,743 --> 00:54:45,849
 Tell me any mother, who would throw her child in the river.

768
00:54:46,346 --> 00:54:47,700
I mean, look at the solution

769
00:54:47,724 --> 00:54:50,236
 if you're afraid from Firaun(فرعون) than do what, throw him in the river.

770
00:54:51,005 --> 00:54:55,486
The solution seems to be worse than the problem, but Allah told her,

771
00:54:55,841 --> 00:54:58,964
وَلَا تَخَافِي وَلَا تَحْزَنِي ۖ إِنَّا رَادُّوهُ إِلَيْكِ وَجَاعِلُوهُ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ۝

772
00:54:58,989 --> 00:55:04,816
If you do that, don't have any fear or sorrow, because he will come back to you and I will make him a messenger.

773
00:55:05,372 --> 00:55:06,843
 Do what I tell you, and that will happen.

774
00:55:07,254 --> 00:55:12,330
She did have Yaqeen(يقين) in Allah and she throw her child, Musa(موسى) the newborn infant in the river.

775
00:55:13,307 --> 00:55:18,118
If she would have kept Musa(موسى) in her arms and not believed in the Promise of Allah

776
00:55:18,533 --> 00:55:21,404
 the soldiers of Firaun(فرعون), his intelligence services

777
00:55:21,623 --> 00:55:24,256
would have discovered that, and they would have killed Musa(موسى)

778
00:55:24,281 --> 00:55:27,901
because he's a male boy born among Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل).

779
00:55:28,632 --> 00:55:32,383
But because she believed in the Promise of Allah he was picked up by a soldier of Allah

780
00:55:32,824 --> 00:55:35,582
the wife of Firaun(فرعون) - she was a soldier of Allah.

781
00:55:36,180 --> 00:55:39,561
And she loved him and she adopted him as her child.

782
00:55:40,386 --> 00:55:43,857
And because Musa(موسى) would breastfeed from no one but his own mother.

783
00:55:45,056 --> 00:55:49,907
Musa(موسى) would be carried to the house of his mother, surrounded by royal guards

784
00:55:50,598 --> 00:55:54,756
and they're paying the mother of Musa(موسى), a salary, a stipend

785
00:55:55,338 --> 00:55:57,240
so that she could breastfeed her own child.

786
00:55:59,237 --> 00:56:01,783
That's because she had Yaqeen(يقين) in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and that's what happened.

787
00:56:02,662 --> 00:56:03,582
 Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

788
00:56:03,686 --> 00:56:07,148
فَٱلْتَقَطَهُۥٓ ءَالُ فِرْعَوْنَ لِيَكُونَ لَهُمْ عَدُوًّا وَحَزَنًا ۗ

789
00:56:07,401 --> 00:56:11,515
The soldiers of Firaun(فرعون) picked up Musa(موسى), but he is going to be their enemy.

790
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:17,309
They didn't know that, they didn’t know that, the child, this, this newborn child that can barely see,

791
00:56:17,901 --> 00:56:19,844
 will be the one who will bring their end.

792
00:56:22,169 --> 00:56:24,553
 That's the result of Yaqeen(يقين) in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

793
00:56:24,956 --> 00:56:28,161
 The army of Usama(أسامه) came back, in a huge celebration.

794
00:56:28,853 --> 00:56:33,416
It was received in Madina - He succeeded - He was victorious.

795
00:56:33,693 --> 00:56:36,832
So the policy of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) did pay.

796
00:56:37,578 --> 00:56:41,288
Now that's why all of the Sahabah(صحابه) after that, they realize that

797
00:56:41,580 --> 00:56:44,809
when Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) say something, just follow it, go ahead with it,

798
00:56:45,767 --> 00:56:50,168
because he has Taeed(تاعيد) of Allah, he has the support of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

799
00:56:51,297 --> 00:56:57,230
Next segment is Huroob-Ar-Riddah(حروب ألردة), the wars of apostasy.

800
00:56:59,078 --> 00:57:03,943
What is the definition of Riddah(ردة), first of all, An-Nawawi(ألنَّووِّي) says;

801
00:57:04,814 --> 00:57:13,560
هي قَطعُ الإسلامِ ،بنيتٍ أو قول كفرٍ ، أو فعلٍ ، سواءٌ قال استهزاءً، أو عِنادً، أو اعتقادً

802
00:57:13,923 --> 00:57:22,604
فمن نفثَّانا أو رسل أو كذب رسولًا أو حلل محرمًا بالإجماع كزن أو عكسه أو نف وجوب

803
00:57:23,020 --> 00:57:28,052
مجمعً عليه أو عكس ذالك أو عزم على الكفر أو ترد فيه كفر

804
00:57:28,875 --> 00:57:34,473
An-Nawawi(ألنَّووِّي) says: Riddah(ردة), the definition of Riddah(ردة) is discontinuing Islam.

805
00:57:35,486 --> 00:57:36,188
 قَطعُ الإسلامِ

806
00:57:36,261 --> 00:57:37,301
You cut Islam

807
00:57:37,365 --> 00:57:43,256
you were a Muslim and then that was discontinued or terminated by the Niyyah(نية).

808
00:57:43,753 --> 00:57:47,045
So if a person has a Niyyah(نية) of leaving Islam, they have left it.

809
00:57:47,963 --> 00:57:50,199
 أو قول كفرٍ

810
00:57:50,477 --> 00:57:54,746
Or a statement, some words can make a person apostate

811
00:57:55,189 --> 00:57:55,982
أو فعلٍ

812
00:57:56,104 --> 00:58:00,200
 Or an action, So sometimes an action could be Riddah(ردة)

813
00:58:00,637 --> 00:58:02,191
سواءٌ قال استهزاءً

814
00:58:02,516 --> 00:58:06,297
Whether that action, or statement was done out of mocking.

815
00:58:07,512 --> 00:58:12,012
Even if it was done out of mocking, if somebody for example makes fun of Rasool Allah ﷺ

816
00:58:12,043 --> 00:58:13,953
and they are just joking - that is Riddah(ردة)

817
00:58:15,301 --> 00:58:16,028
أو عِنادًا

818
00:58:16,119 --> 00:58:17,804
Or out of stubbornness

819
00:58:18,217 --> 00:58:19,102
أو اعتقادًا

820
00:58:19,142 --> 00:58:20,341
Or out of belief

821
00:58:21,551 --> 00:58:25,411
And then he says, and if you make a Halal(حلال), Haram(حرام) or a Haram(حرام), Halal(حلال)

822
00:58:25,548 --> 00:58:26,953
 that is also Riddah(ردة).

823
00:58:28,699 --> 00:58:32,261
Or has the intention of becoming a Murtadd(مرتد)

824
00:58:33,427 --> 00:58:35,657
or was debating whether to do it or not

825
00:58:35,681 --> 00:58:38,901
 for example, I'm not sure whether I want to do it or not, that is Riddah(ردة).

826
00:58:39,867 --> 00:58:41,645
So that's the definition of Riddah(ردة).

827
00:58:43,178 --> 00:58:44,809
Riddah(ردة) comes in different forms

828
00:58:44,833 --> 00:58:48,819
For example, not applying the Hukum(حكم) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

829
00:58:48,837 --> 00:58:49,535
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

830
00:58:49,559 --> 00:58:52,776
وَمَنْ لَمْ يَحْكُمْ بِمَا أَنزَلَ اللَّهُ فَأُوْلَئِكَ هُمُ الْكَافِرُونَ۝

831
00:58:53,428 --> 00:58:58,916
Anybody who does not apply the law of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, the rules of Allah has become a Murtadd(مرتد)

832
00:58:59,223 --> 00:59:00,252
فَأُوْلَئِكَ هُمُ الْكَافِرُونَ

833
00:59:00,276 --> 00:59:01,352
They are the disbelievers.

834
00:59:01,645 --> 00:59:04,555
Another common form Riddah(ردة) today, is

835
00:59:04,594 --> 00:59:11,054
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنْ تُطِيعُوا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا يَرُدُّوكُمْ عَلَى أَعْقَابِكُمْ فَتَنْقَلِبُوا خَاسِرِينَ۝

836
00:59:11,446 --> 00:59:16,436
O you, who believe, if you follow the way of the disbelievers

837
00:59:16,887 --> 00:59:21,467
They will make you retreat, Riddah(ردة) means retreat.

838
00:59:21,729 --> 00:59:23,185
يَرُدُّوكُمْ عَلَى أَعْقَابِكُمْ

839
00:59:23,463 --> 00:59:24,714
They will make you retreat.

840
00:59:25,077 --> 00:59:26,419
فَتَنْقَلِبُوا خَاسِرِينَ

841
00:59:26,572 --> 00:59:28,813
And you will become the losers, and Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

842
00:59:28,845 --> 00:59:31,550
ومن يتولهم منكم فإنه منهم

843
00:59:32,093 --> 00:59:36,700
Whoever follows their way, becomes one of them.

844
00:59:36,853 --> 00:59:39,658
And this is an Ayah(آية) Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث)

845
00:59:40,116 --> 00:59:43,092
 that if you love a people, then you will be with them.

846
00:59:45,268 --> 00:59:49,038
The categories of Riddah(ردة) in the time of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه,

847
00:59:49,339 --> 00:59:50,206
there were three types.

848
00:59:50,243 --> 00:59:51,681
Al-Qadhi Ayyaz(ألقاضي عيَّاض) says;

849
00:59:51,908 --> 00:59:54,351
صنف عادوا إلى عبادة ألأوسان

850
00:59:54,933 --> 00:59:58,419
The first type: These people, they went back to worshipping idols

851
00:59:58,525 --> 01:00:02,783
 they went back to what they were doing before Islam, pagan worshipping.

852
01:00:03,990 --> 01:00:04,652
The second type,

853
01:00:04,867 --> 01:00:09,656
وصنفٌ تبع  مسيلمة ولأسود ألعنسي وكل منهم مدع من النبوة

854
01:00:10,034 --> 01:00:15,168
The second type of Murtaddeen(مرتدين) are the ones, who followed Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمه ألكذاب) and Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسودألعنسي)

855
01:00:15,443 --> 01:00:17,332
and these two men claim to be prophets

856
01:00:17,812 --> 01:00:19,714
so this was the second type of Riddah(ردة).

857
01:00:19,912 --> 01:00:20,956
The third type;

858
01:00:21,936 --> 01:00:29,545
وصنفٌ ثالث لإستمرُّ على الإسلام ولكنهم جهد زكوة وتأول باَنَّ خاصه من زمن النبي

859
01:00:29,939 --> 01:00:34,347
The third type of Murtaddeen(مرتدين), they remained Muslims they were still Muslims,

860
01:00:34,762 --> 01:00:36,758
 but they refused to pay the Zaka'a(زكوة)

861
01:00:37,465 --> 01:00:40,855
because they said that Zaka'a(زكوة) should only be paid to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

862
01:00:41,672 --> 01:00:44,811
These were considered to be Murtaddeen(مرتدين) even though they used to pray

863
01:00:44,836 --> 01:00:47,086
 and they were continuing on the Ibadaat(عبادات) of Islam.

864
01:00:47,111 --> 01:00:49,509
The only problem was they refused to pay Zaka'a(زكوة).

865
01:00:49,982 --> 01:00:52,776
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه consider them to be Murtadd(مرتد)

866
01:00:52,800 --> 01:00:55,112
and we'll talk about that in the next session.

867
01:00:56,147 --> 01:00:57,441
When did Riddah(ردَّة) start.?

868
01:00:57,715 --> 01:00:59,910
Riddah(ردَّة) actually started in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

869
01:00:59,955 --> 01:01:01,366
 and not in the time of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

870
01:01:02,168 --> 01:01:10,857
In the 10th year of Hijrah(هجرة), when Rasool Allah ﷺ his reign was spreading all over.

871
01:01:11,779 --> 01:01:13,812
 You had all of these weak hearted people,

872
01:01:14,464 --> 01:01:17,942
who joined Islam just because of the fear of the sword

873
01:01:18,281 --> 01:01:22,901
just because Islam was strong, they became Muslim, these are the Munafiqeen(مُنافقين),

874
01:01:22,938 --> 01:01:26,214
 they don't really believe in it inside.

875
01:01:27,328 --> 01:01:28,642
 They are just riding the wave.

876
01:01:29,795 --> 01:01:32,365
Prophethood was not something known among the Arabs before

877
01:01:33,690 --> 01:01:38,157
but now, when some people saw the success of the mission of Muhammadﷺ.

878
01:01:38,389 --> 01:01:40,755
They said: Hey, why don't we also claim to be prophets

879
01:01:41,189 --> 01:01:44,594
nobody before Muhammadﷺ in Arabia, has ever claimed to be a prophet.

880
01:01:46,442 --> 01:01:52,543
But when the Arabs saw that Muhammadﷺ became the undisputed leader of Arabia.

881
01:01:52,891 --> 01:01:54,844
 They said: Well let's give it a shot.

882
01:01:55,435 --> 01:01:58,115
So, Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب), Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

883
01:01:58,341 --> 01:02:00,469
 and Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي) and Sajjah(سجَّاح)

884
01:02:00,854 --> 01:02:02,731
they all claimed to be Prophets three men and one woman.

885
01:02:03,762 --> 01:02:07,205
The most dangerous of the four were Musailimah(مسيلمة), and Al-Aswad(ألأسود).

886
01:02:07,229 --> 01:02:09,633
Musailimah(مسيلمة) in Yamamah(يمامه) and Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) in Yemen(يمن).

887
01:02:10,450 --> 01:02:16,069
These two, they were rising and their danger was expanding so fast

888
01:02:16,676 --> 01:02:24,647
 that they were amassing huge armies that were beginning to make a real threat against the Muslims.

889
01:02:25,343 --> 01:02:28,372
 Both Musailimah(مسيلمة) and Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

890
01:02:28,469 --> 01:02:31,972
 claimed to be prophets during the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ in the 10th year,

891
01:02:32,806 --> 01:02:34,254
in the 10th year of Hijrah(هجرة).

892
01:02:35,246 --> 01:02:37,629
But Rasool Allah ﷺ saw a dream before he passed away.

893
01:02:38,383 --> 01:02:43,780
He said: I saw, as if I was wearing two bracelets of gold.

894
01:02:44,231 --> 01:02:48,169
رَأَيْتُ أنَّ في زراية سِوارَيْنِ مِن ذَهَبٍ، فكرحتُهُما

895
01:02:48,370 --> 01:02:49,580
And I disliked that.

896
01:02:50,160 --> 01:02:51,009
فَنَفَخْتُهُما

897
01:02:51,049 --> 01:02:53,649
So, I blew at them, and they flew away.

898
01:02:54,086 --> 01:02:59,279
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: My interpretation is that the two bracelets are

899
01:02:59,408 --> 01:03:01,653
the liar of Yamamah(يمامه) and the liar of Yemen.

900
01:03:01,845 --> 01:03:04,703
Rasool Ullah would call them only by this title, liar.

901
01:03:05,424 --> 01:03:07,769
The liar of Yamamah(يمامه) and the liar of Yemen.

902
01:03:08,703 --> 01:03:11,025
Rasool Ullah is seeing two bracelets

903
01:03:11,393 --> 01:03:14,671
bracelets, surrounding the arm meaning,

904
01:03:14,805 --> 01:03:18,738
these two will be a danger on the community because there was Tulaiha(طليحة), a third prophet,

905
01:03:19,016 --> 01:03:21,146
 but Rasool Allah ﷺ only saw two bracelets

906
01:03:21,274 --> 01:03:24,243
 meaning these two are going to be the most dangerous two.

907
01:03:24,550 --> 01:03:25,436
فكرھتُهُما

908
01:03:25,682 --> 01:03:29,840
I disliked them. And Rasool Allah ﷺ said: They were gold.

909
01:03:30,033 --> 01:03:36,557
Gold stands for the Zenah(زينة) of this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) attachment to this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

910
01:03:36,592 --> 01:03:41,666
 So Musailima(مسيلمة) and Al-Aswad(ألأسود) were not doing this not for Al-Aakhira(ألآخرة), they were doing it for Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

911
01:03:42,102 --> 01:03:46,487
And in general, gold carries negative connotations in dreams.

912
01:03:48,116 --> 01:03:52,912
The blowing of Rasool Allah ﷺ means that even though these are very dangerous

913
01:03:52,973 --> 01:03:56,266
Both of them are very dangerous, meaning they are surrounded both his arms.

914
01:03:56,972 --> 01:04:00,168
But the fact that by just blowing at them they flew away

915
01:04:00,569 --> 01:04:03,156
means that even though they will become very strong,

916
